    {
      "part_type": "reading",
      "part_name": "III. 閱讀測驗 (第 31-33 題)",
      "instruction": "說明：以下有三篇短文，共有十個問題...",
      "has_passage": true,
      "passage": "<p class='mb-4'>Most heroes are people like you. But what makes them heroes? They find special courage when they need it. They are brave enough to help in an emergency while others may stand by. A hero sees what needs to be done and does it.</p><p class='mb-4'>Sometimes heroes are rewarded for their brave acts. One such reward is the Carnegie Medal. It is given to people who act bravely and face danger to save the lives of others...</p>",
      "passage_translation": "<p class='mb-4'>大多數的英雄都是像你一樣的普通人。但什麼讓他們成為英雄呢？他們在需要時會找到特別的勇氣。在緊急情況下，當其他人可能袖手旁觀時，他們夠勇敢去幫忙。英雄看見需要做的事並且付諸實行。</p><p class='mb-4'>有時候英雄會因為他們的勇敢行為而獲得報償。其中一種報償就是卡內基獎章。它頒發給那些勇敢行動並面對危險以拯救他人生命的人...</p>",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q_num": 31,
          "question": "The Carnegie Medal is given to those who are _______",
          "options": {
            "A": "sick and poor.",
            "B": "rich and famous.",
            "C": "young and brave.",
            "D": "unselfish and courageous."
          },
          "correct_answer": "D",
          "explanation": {
            "translation": "卡內基獎章頒發給那些 _______ 的人。",
            "analysis": "文章第二段提到：'It is given to people who act bravely and face danger to save the lives of others.' (頒給那些勇敢行動、面對危險以拯救他人的人)。拯救他人即是 unselfish (無私的)，勇敢面對危險即是 courageous (有勇氣的)。",
            "vocab": [
